@page
@model SettingsModel
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Settings"; }
<div class="page-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Policy and configuration status</p><h1>Settings</h1></div><a asp-page="/Maintenance">Maintenance</a></div>
<div asp-validation-summary="All" class="notice"></div>
<section class="band"><h2>Explicit investment limits</h2>
	<p>Each save creates a new portfolio revision and incremented policy version, with pending research pinned to that revision. Existing ledger, snapshot, reconciliation and historical run inputs are unchanged.</p>
	<form method="post" asp-page-handler="Policy">
		<input type="hidden" asp-for="ExpectedRevision" />
		<p><label asp-for="MaximumPositionPercent">Maximum position (%)</label><input asp-for="MaximumPositionPercent" type="number" min="0" max="100" step="any" /><span asp-validation-for="MaximumPositionPercent"></span></p>
		<p><label asp-for="MaximumTacticalPercent">Maximum tactical allocation (%) / optional</label><input asp-for="MaximumTacticalPercent" type="number" min="0" max="100" step="any" /><span asp-validation-for="MaximumTacticalPercent"></span></p>
		<p><label><input asp-for="AcceptInformationalPolicy" /> I explicitly choose these limits and acknowledge that policy remains informational. Saving queues research but does not implement sizing, establish suitability or authorize a trade.</label></p>
		<button type="submit">Save policy</button>
	</form>
	<p class="muted">No numerical defaults are supplied. Blank tactical allocation remains unconfigured. Missing scenario inputs and sizing still block actionable eligibility.</p>
</section>
<section class="band"><h2>Investment policy</h2><p class="notice">@(Model.Portfolio.Policy.Configured ? "Configured policy is stored with the confirmed revision." : "Unconfigured: no numerical investment policy, suitability or sized actions are authorized.")</p><p>Balanced long-term and tactical research does not imply numerical limits. Technical execution budgets below are not investment rules.</p><dl class="manifest"><dt>Policy version</dt><dd>@Model.Portfolio.Policy.Version</dd><dt>Independent holdings reconciliation</dt><dd>Unavailable / actual statement formats unverified</dd></dl></section>
<section class="band"><h2>Runtime and identity</h2><dl class="manifest"><dt>Environment</dt><dd>@Model.EnvironmentName</dd><dt>Authentication</dt><dd>@Model.Authentication</dd><dt>Execution mode</dt><dd>@Model.Runtime.Mode</dd><dt>Model binding</dt><dd>@Model.Runtime.ModelBinding</dd><dt>Availability diagnostic</dt><dd>@Model.Runtime.Diagnostic</dd><dt>Live authorized</dt><dd>@Model.Runtime.LiveAuthorized</dd><dt>Schedule</dt><dd>08:00 Europe/Vilnius, every day. Worker must be invoked by the configured schedule or on demand.</dd><dt>Secrets</dt><dd>Not displayed. Model/provider adapters run only in the worker.</dd></dl></section>
<section class="band"><h2>Technical limits</h2><dl class="manifest"><dt>Run / monthly AI budget</dt><dd>USD @Display.Number(Model.Runtime.Limits.PerRunUsd) / USD @Display.Number(Model.Runtime.Limits.MonthlyAiUsd)</dd><dt>Maximum call reservation</dt><dd>USD @Display.Number(Model.Runtime.Limits.MaximumCallUsd)</dd><dt>Decisions / research tasks / critic passes</dt><dd>@Model.Runtime.Limits.MaximumDecisions / @Model.Runtime.Limits.MaximumResearchTasks / @Model.Runtime.Limits.MaximumCriticPasses</dd><dt>Tools / model submissions</dt><dd>@Model.Runtime.Limits.MaximumTools / @Model.Runtime.Limits.MaximumModelSubmissions</dd><dt>Deadline / output tokens</dt><dd>@Model.Runtime.Limits.MaximumRunMinutes minutes / @Model.Runtime.Limits.MaximumOutputTokens tokens per reply</dd><dt>Run / call token ceiling</dt><dd>@Model.Runtime.Limits.MaximumRunTokens / @Model.Runtime.Limits.MaximumCallTokens</dd></dl><p class="muted">Reservations constrain discretionary AI calls. They are not a hard cap on platform billing, retained storage, subscriptions or tax.</p></section>
<section class="band"><h2>Research catalog</h2><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Canonical instrument</th><th>Symbol</th><th>Exchange / currency</th><th>Kind / sector</th></tr></thead><tbody>@foreach (var instrument in Model.Runtime.CandidateCatalog) { <tr><td>@instrument.Id</td><td>@instrument.Symbol</td><td>@instrument.Exchange / @instrument.Currency</td><td>@instrument.Kind / @instrument.Sector</td></tr> }</tbody></table></div><p class="muted">Catalog inclusion is a research scope decision, not verification of ownership or brokerage eligibility.</p></section>